## Common Patterns & Anti-Patterns

### ✅ Do
- Use domain events for state changes
- Check state before firing events (avoid duplicate events)
- Use value objects for type safety
- Validate permissions in handlers
- Use specifications for filtering
- Follow CQRS pattern strictly
- Keep domain policies pure (no dependencies)

### ❌ Don't
- Don't update tank fuel levels from deliveries
- Don't add infrastructure dependencies to domain layer
- Don't use synchronous I/O in async contexts
- Don't bypass permission checks
- Don't mix read and write models
- Don't fire domain events on every method call (only on state changes)
- Don't use `var` when type is not evident

